GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC9 §4, UC11): the overworld's side strips show only its scene.

- GPU3D: WideField, set by GoldLink each frame while the game is in the overworld. Then, past
  the DS's own view, untextured polygons are skipped: ground the game draws without ever
  loading its material (a neighbouring map's, as no one could see it), plain white or grey.
- GPU2D_Soft: then the main engine's side strips (with the 3D layer on) are composed without
  BG1-3: there the game's 2D layers are its interface (text boxes, a town's banner), and their
  tiles past the screen's edges were never meant to be seen. The 3D scene and sprites stay.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

--- a/src/GPU3D.h	2026-11-12 22:00:17.417024111 -0500
+++ b/src/GPU3D.h	2026-11-12 22:00:17.426165988 -0500
@@ -235,6 +235,10 @@
     // Position tests are left alone: the game reads their results back.
     static constexpr int MaxWideSide = 64;
     int WideSide = 0;
+    // GoldLink: the game is in the overworld (set by GoldLink each frame). Its 2D layers are its
+    // interface there (text boxes, a town's banner): their tiles past the screen's edges were
+    // never meant to be seen, so the side strips leave them out (the 3D scene and sprites stay).
+    bool WideField = false;
     bool WideActive() const noexcept
     {
         return WideSide > 0 && Viewport[0] == 0 && Viewport[4] == 256;
